  "title": "Interneurons: The Brain's Connectors",
  "emoji": "⚡",
  "color": "#8B5CF6",
  "description": "A fast breakdown of Interneurons: The Brain's Connectors for builders.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Interneurons never leave the brain or spinal cord. They're the middlemen connecting everything.",
      "visual": "🔀"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "They relay signals between sensory and motor neurons, enabling reflexes and complex circuits.",
      "visual": "🔄"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "Over 99% of all neurons in your body are interneurons—they vastly outnumber the other types.",
      "visual": "📊"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Many interneurons are inhibitory, using GABA to fine-tune and regulate neural circuits.",
      "visual": "🎛️"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "The incredible complexity of human thought exists because interneurons create layered processing networks.",
      "visual": "🕸️"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Interneurons are invisible to the outside world but run the show inside.",
      "visual": "🎭"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What percentage of neurons are interneurons?",
    "options": [
      "Over 99%",
      "About 50%",
      "Less than 10%"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
